      "problem": "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y-8)^{2}}{48}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y-8)^{2}}{48}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=4$ and $k=8.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(4,8).$",
